{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/376918-abyssal-charm-concept-willpower-damage","id":376918,"title":"Abyssal charm concept: willpower damage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-20T22:08:41-08:00","id":376918,"title":"Abyssal charm concept: willpower damage","content":"&quot;Screaming Nightmares Silenced&quot;<br /> <br /> Presence [X] Essence [X]<br /> Cost: [X] Motes [X] Willpower<br /> Type: Simple; Duration: Varies<br /> Prerequisites: [X]<br /> <br /> 'The deathknight's arguments strike at the exposed heart of their intended target, shaking their confidence and beliefs to the core. This charm is a dramatic action requiring that the deathknight speak against an intimacy they already know their target to have, employing either grim logic or fierce intimidation. Roll the deathknight's Manipulation or Charisma + Presence against the target's MDV. Threshold successes are rolled again, with successes applied as &quot;damage&quot; to the target's temporary willpower track, marked using an &quot;x&quot; to distinguish them from spent willpower. The target heals this psychic damage at a rate of one per night of full rest. A target reduced to zero temporary willpower while under the effects of this charm does not become catatonic as normal. Instead the targeted intimacy is perfectly eroded and any willpower damaged by this charm is healed and restored, bringing a sense of both loss and catharsis. Victims of this charm's effects may voluntarily shed the targeted intimacy at any time to heal any remaining willpower damage. An Essence [X] Presence [X] repurchase allows the deathknight to instead replace the targeted intimacy with an intimacy of their choosing, determined at the time this charm is cast.'<br /> <br /> Opinions welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 01-21-2015, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T22:32:25-08:00","id":376947,"title":"","content":"Nice, very nice. I think it's Essence 2-3. And one question- can you spend number of willpower to resist the attack (as most of the mental attacking charms)?<br /> Edit: And I'm not understand why this is a dramatic action and not simple action in social combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4614-og-barbari","name":"Og Barbari","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T22:49:54-08:00","id":376961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Og Barbari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/376918-abyssal-charm-concept-willpower-damage?p=376947#post376947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice, very nice. I think it's Essence 2-3. And one question- can you spend number of willpower to resist the attack (as most of the mental attacking charms)?<br /> Edit: And I'm not understand why this is a dramatic action and not simple action in social combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, good question. On the one hand that would be the nice thing to do, but on the other if you can get out of taking lasting willpower damage by spending temporary willpower, I'm concerned the charm will become toothless. Perhaps it would be keep the essence requirement high but leave out a willpower resist option?<br /> <br /> One very important question is whether or not this charm should be stackable. If not then a simple social combat action would be fine, but if so I think a dramatic action might be best to keep it from being easily spammable. Or perhaps it's stackable but targets become immune for a period following the loss of their intimacy. Thoughts on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T00:02:35-08:00","id":377016,"title":"","content":"Very nice concept. I think it should be atleast essence 3. Willpower resist option would invalidate the charm, because spenting temp. willpower to avoid losing them for a few days is no choice at all. If you want to put an resist option, it could be HL cost. Instead of taking temp willpower damage, the target could opt to lose health levels.<br /> <br /> Recovery time should be dependant the type of the target, mortals should heal slower and exalted should heal faster.<br /> <br /> Charm also needs Combo-Basic and Shaping keywords.<br /> <br /> You can also add an expension charm that allows the abyssal to harvest motes from the willpower drain later on; making them pyschic vampires :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T08:14:27-08:00","id":377247,"title":"","content":"I am not sure on the shaping keyword. I am thinking maybe crippling like the charms that stop natural healing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T10:59:09-08:00","id":377364,"title":"","content":"HL cost is a good option, but I had thought that the voluntary intimacy loss would be a sufficient &quot;easy out.&quot; It all depends on what intimacy is targeted, though. In Ex2 all intimacies carry the same weight unless powered/protected by charms. There have been murmurings that Ex3 might be using them differently so I might do a redraft of this when we have those rules. For now it might be best to see this as a simple charm which either removes an intimacy as a simple action or does lasting willpower damage.<br /> <br /> I think crippling rather than shaping is a good idea, as I don't imagine this as shaping thoughts so much as creating such incredibly compelling arguments that they can do real damage to a person's psyche. These are the sort of words that force you to reconsider your entire meaning for living, and until you've either had time to process them or accepted their truth your brain is in shambles.<br /> <br /> I think including a period of &quot;immunity&quot; after losing an intimacy to this charm would help balance it but I'm unsure how much time to allow. Perhaps one day of immunity per point of permanent willpower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T13:40:53-08:00","id":377512,"title":"","content":"Yeah, crippling works too, i though it as shaping the person's body and removing the ability to recover his will back. But problem with cripling is, you gonna need resistance charms to resist this and it feels wrong. It should be Integrity that should govern psyche of a character, not resistance. So a charm that makes your arm un-broken will contest this charm, and that seems strange.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T14:13:33-08:00","id":377531,"title":"","content":"hmm, you make a good point. Certainly I'm fine with most medicine charms (which are generally also treated as psychiatric) working on these lost levels, but it would be strange to see a Lunar shrugging this off with Limb-Replacing Prana or whatever. Since it is mental influence integrity charms and perfect mental defenses still apply to it though. If nothing else, making it crippling makes it easier to shrug off rather than less. Perhaps on that note I should include one of the mental keywords, but is this an emotion effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T14:43:04-08:00","id":377548,"title":"","content":"Making it Shaping pretty much makes it ineffective due to 2e's ridiculous design philosophy re Shaping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T15:39:56-08:00","id":377567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/376918-abyssal-charm-concept-willpower-damage?p=377548#post377548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making it Shaping pretty much makes it ineffective due to 2e's ridiculous design philosophy re Shaping.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My current character has no shaping defense...I like to live dangerously...quack","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T19:05:26-08:00","id":377710,"title":"","content":"Well fixing psyche is also in presence. Anyway I do agree that crippling making it resisted with resistance charms is weird the issue with shaping is why I was hoping to avoid it in so far as if it ha that tag it wouldn't see much of any play or use. I am wondering if compulsion or emotion might be enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T19:12:40-08:00","id":377716,"title":"","content":"I don't think it particularly needs a Keyword - a social perfect negates it regardless. <br /> <br /> But if anything I'd put it as Emotion based on the description of how it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T10:46:45-08:00","id":378195,"title":"","content":"I think an Emotion keyword would be appropriate, and although crippling would be appropriate the implications that has for certain resistance charms is throwing me off. If we don't include a crippling keyword but treat this effect as a natural mental influence would it still be balanced around essence 3 you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T10:49:56-08:00","id":378198,"title":"","content":"Honestly it'd be crap as NMI given the rules for how often you have to pay to resist NMI, and the low cost to resist NMI.<br /> <br /> I agree that Crippling is an imperfect fit because of how the rules seem to present it as physical-injuries-only. So Emotion is probably your best bet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T11:53:01-08:00","id":379274,"title":"","content":"Although I still need to consider a few thigns before I finish my write-up, a big thanks to everyone here for your suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T00:11:45-08:00","id":379889,"title":"","content":"Just occured to me, since this is a new concept; you can just invent a new keyword : E-Crippling as in E-mail but E stands for Emotion :P<br /> <br /> Do post the final version here please i am curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T00:36:05-08:00","id":379894,"title":"","content":"In first edition there was a non-homebrew Abyssal Charm called <b>Soul-Flaying Gaze</b> that seems relevant to bring up:<br /> <br /> <b>Soul-Flaying Gaze</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8 motes, 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One turn<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Minimum Presence:</b> 4<br /> <b>Minimum Essence:</b> 3<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Elegant Tyrant's Majesty<br /> By staring intently at a target, an Abyssal with this Charm can sap that victim's will and subjugate her spirit. The target must be within five yards and must be able to see the Exalt when Soul-Flaying Gaze is invoked. If these conditions are met, the target finds her vision drawn to the deathknights own eyes.<br /> <br /> As their gazes connect, the Abyssal's player rolls Manipulation + Presence in a resisted roll against the target's Willpower. If the Exalt wins, the target is immediately entranced and can take no further actions that turn. Additionally, the victim loses a number of points of Willpower equal to the Abyssal's permanent Essence. If the target wins, the Charm has no effect. A character who loses all Willpower from this Charm becomes highly suggestible to the Abyssal. Although she cannot be ordered to do anything to harm herself or others (unless naturally predisposed to do so), such a hapless individual otherwise obeys the Exalt for the rest of the scene. This control shatters immediately if the victim suffers actual damage, although she must regain lost Willpower normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}